{
  "title": "s3g Thru",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Getting started",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "First sound",
          "lines": [
            "Track 1-4 selects a",
            "lane. Shift + Track",
            "opens its sample",
            "browser. Turn the",
            "main encoder to",
            "browse; click to load",
            "a WAV.",
            "",
            "Press note pads to",
            "play. Fill other lanes",
            "before scanning",
            "across them: an empty",
            "lane is silent."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pages and knobs",
          "lines": [
            "Menu opens parameter",
            "pages. The eight",
            "screen cells match",
            "knobs 1-8. Up/Down",
            "stays in that page",
            "bank.",
            "",
            "Hold Capture and",
            "press Track 1 Voice,",
            "2 Lane, 3 Mix/FX, or",
            "4 Performance. Repeat",
            "the chord to advance",
            "within that bank.",
            "",
            "Capture + Menu opens",
            "the hub. Track 1-4",
            "opens a bank. Turn,",
            "then click a page.",
            "Back returns page to",
            "bank, hub, prior view.",
            "ALL",
            "shows the full list."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pads and hold",
          "lines": [
            "In Keys mode, Up/Down",
            "changes octave on the",
            "waveform page. Pads &",
            "Scale sets Root, Scale",
            "and pad mode.",
            "",
            "Shift + pad toggles a",
            "held note. Hold Off",
            "chooses manual",
            "release or an",
            "automatic delay. In",
            "Cues mode, Shift +",
            "pad stores a cue",
            "instead.",
            "",
            "Amp Envelope sets",
            "attack, decay, sustain",
            "and release. Pad",
            "velocity does not set",
            "sample volume."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "OXI E16 control",
          "lines": [
            "Remote THRU RM scene.",
            "Use matching Thru",
            "module and scene.",
            "",
            "Schwung Surface:",
            "E16. USB1.",
            "USB Multi Port Off.",
            "USB MIDI Thru Off.",
            "",
            "Hold E16 Shift and",
            "turn dial 1 for pages.",
            "1 Engine, 2 Stack,",
            "3-6 Engine details,",
            "7 Sends/Priority,",
            "8 Color,",
            "9 Rotary, 10 Delay,",
            "11 Reverb, 12 Tape.",
            "",
            "Shift + dial 2 press:",
            "opens Page Jump.",
            "Release Shift; press",
            "dials 1-12 to jump.",
            "Dial 16 cancels.",
            "",
            "Top rows A/C.",
            "Bottom rows B/D.",
            "Quad: Shift + dial 1",
            "press switches C/D.",
            "",
            "Names above values:",
            "values and units.",
            "Hold dial while turn:",
            "fine adjustment.",
            "",
            "Unused controls show",
            "a small square.",
            "ALG/text choices:",
            "changed pixels only.",
            "Header updates first.",
            "All 12 page positions",
            "remain fixed.",
            "",
            "Ring A neutral;",
            "Split B teal, Shared",
            "B plum. Quad C yellow,",
            "D plum. Return purple.",
            "",
            "THRU RM stays blank:",
            "versions, USB and",
            "Surface E16. Select",
            "the script-free scene",
            "before takeover.",
            "",
            "Move Shift + Menu:",
            "E16 Link 5/5. STATE,",
            "LAST, ACK/NACK and",
            "PENDING PX.",
            "Counts are not audio",
            "load measurements."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "MIDI controllers",
          "lines": [
            "Menu: MIDI Control.",
            "MODE: Auto, NRPN, CC,",
            "MNLT, E16, E+M, Off.",
            "",
            "E+M: native relative",
            "CC on E16; Monolit",
            "absolute CC via TRS.",
            "Use Surface CC Only",
            "and scene THRU EM.",
            "Rings show actual",
            "Thru values.",
            "",
            "E16 Remote is a",
            "separate readable",
            "controller option."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Engine List",
          "lines": [
            "Pads & Scale: ENGS",
            "LIST enables Voice",
            "Engines and Voice",
            "Setup. ORDR adds",
            "Cycle Up, Cycle Down",
            "and Shuffle.",
            "",
            "Setup ASSN chooses",
            "Touch, Degree or",
            "Register. Degree",
            "follows the scale;",
            "Register divides the",
            "keyboard range.",
            "",
            "Turn the main",
            "encoder to pick an",
            "entry. Click for its",
            "engine pages; Back",
            "returns. Held notes",
            "keep their engine."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Keyboard engines",
          "lines": [
            "Menu: Pads & Scale.",
            "Set knob 1 PADS to",
            "KEYS and knob 7 ENGS",
            "to LIST. Choose Root",
            "and Scale.",
            "",
            "Voice Engines: knobs",
            "assign an engine to",
            "each available",
            "entry.",
            "",
            "Voice Setup: knob 2",
            "ASSN chooses DEGR or",
            "REG. DEGR follows",
            "scale degrees. REG",
            "divides the keyboard",
            "pitch range from low",
            "to high.",
            "",
            "The same note keeps",
            "its engine role",
            "across playing",
            "orders. Several",
            "notes may use one",
            "entry. Choose TOUCH",
            "to use ORDR again."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Entry variations",
          "lines": [
            "Voice Setup: EDIT",
            "picks an entry.",
            "OCTV, SPOS, STAK and",
            "PAN shape new notes.",
            "Existing notes keep",
            "their values.",
            "",
            "SPOS offsets launch",
            "phase, including",
            "full-width regions.",
            "STAK offsets the",
            "scan or chosen lane.",
            "Quad reserves STAK.",
            "",
            "DPTH sets pressure",
            "depth for the part.",
            "In ONE mode it is on",
            "Pads & Scale. Entry",
            "values save with",
            "recorded notes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pressure play",
          "lines": [
            "Pads & Scale PRES",
            "chooses pressure",
            "behavior for the",
            "part. CHAR follows",
            "each played note and",
            "its assigned engine.",
            "",
            "DPTH is shared by",
            "the part: Pads &",
            "Scale in ONE, Voice",
            "Setup in LIST. EDIT",
            "selects the entry",
            "you are editing.",
            "",
            "BRAKE: keep the note",
            "held, press harder",
            "to catch its lane",
            "scan, then relax to",
            "resume. Audio keeps",
            "playing; other notes",
            "keep scanning.",
            "",
            "Higher DPTH makes",
            "the catch easier.",
            "Loop holds the whole",
            "part. Quad uses OFF",
            "or CHAR.",
            "",
            "Pressure gestures",
            "are recorded,",
            "including MIDI poly",
            "aftertouch. Choose",
            "pressure mode and",
            "depth before",
            "recording."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "MIDI notes",
          "lines": [
            "Capture + Menu: MIDI.",
            "Open MIDI Notes 2/3.",
            "",
            "ROUT Parts: channels",
            "1 A, 2 B, 3 C, 4 D.",
            "Single: A only.",
            "Focus: CHAN plays",
            "the selected part.",
            "",
            "Bank B: notes 60-75",
            "play slots 1-16.",
            "Empty slots silent.",
            "",
            "Slices engine:",
            "Root key: slice 1.",
            "Each semitone above",
            "selects next slice.",
            "Wraps at last slice.",
            "Below Root: slice 1.",
            "Keys keep SPEED;",
            "bend still retunes.",
            "",
            "VOICE: Poly, Mono or",
            "Legato, with any Move",
            "pad layout. Non-key",
            "pads stay separate.",
            "",
            "CC64: sustain pedal.",
            "BEND: range 0-24 st.",
            "WHEL: Off, Stack or",
            "Character. VELO sets",
            "external key volume",
            "response, default 0.",
            "",
            "Notes and expression",
            "record into clips.",
            "",
            "USB keys play Thru",
            "without native Move",
            "doubling the notes.",
            "Track MIDI Out is",
            "not needed.",
            "",
            "Native Move tracks:",
            "MIDI In + Out Off.",
            "Clock sync is a",
            "separate setting.",
            "",
            "Note off starts REL.",
            "FX tails may remain.",
            "Stack Hold or Brake",
            "can pause lane scan."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "MIDI sync",
          "lines": [
            "USB keyboard or",
            "OXI One to Move USB.",
            "OXI USB output:",
            "channels 1-4.",
            "",
            "For external clock:",
            "Move MIDI Sync In,",
            "Link Off. MIDI Notes",
            "SYNC Move.",
            "",
            "RUN Tempo Only keeps",
            "clip control local.",
            "Follow Clips: Start",
            "resets, Stop pauses,",
            "Continue resumes.",
            "",
            "Stop or clock loss",
            "releases MIDI keys.",
            "Move pad latches",
            "remain held.",
            "Send Start/Continue",
            "to resume clips."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Samples",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Load a WAV",
          "lines": [
            "Shift + Track 1-4",
            "opens the browser",
            "for that lane. Choose",
            "Move Samples or Thru",
            "Recordings.",
            "",
            "Main turn or Up/Down",
            "selects. A highlighted",
            "WAV auditions at",
            "Preview Level. Click",
            "to load; Back goes up",
            "or closes the",
            "browser.",
            "",
            "Mono and stereo WAVs",
            "load. The lane",
            "capacity is 12",
            "seconds; longer files",
            "are truncated."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Stereo recording",
          "lines": [
            "Choose Move mic or",
            "line input and its",
            "hardware input gain",
            "first. Use headphones",
            "for mic recording.",
            "",
            "Track 1-4 selects the",
            "destination. Shift +",
            "Record starts and",
            "stops stereo audio",
            "capture. The take",
            "becomes that lane",
            "source.",
            "",
            "Mix / Rec sets SRC,",
            "Record Gain and",
            "Monitor. Keep Monitor",
            "at zero unless direct",
            "monitoring is wanted.",
            "SRC can also resample",
            "the mix or a part."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Saved takes",
          "lines": [
            "Completed captures",
            "and sample edits",
            "create new WAVs in",
            "Thru Recordings. A",
            "later recording",
            "replaces the lane",
            "assignment and keeps",
            "the older file.",
            "",
            "Each clip recalls its",
            "own source",
            "assignments. Undo can",
            "restore the latest",
            "source change. Wait",
            "for saving to finish",
            "before powering off."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Sample editing",
          "lines": [
            "Select the lane with",
            "Track, then open its",
            "Sample page. Trim,",
            "Reverse, Normalize",
            "and Fade act on that",
            "lane.",
            "",
            "Turn an action",
            "encoder to apply it.",
            "Each committed edit",
            "saves a new WAV. Stop",
            "recording before",
            "using Undo to restore",
            "the latest edit."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lanes and engines",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Waveform controls",
          "lines": [
            "POS moves the source",
            "window; FLD sets its",
            "width. The waveforms",
            "zoom to that region.",
            "SPD sets transport",
            "speed; note pitch is",
            "additional.",
            "",
            "Where available, STAK",
            "sets the stack start",
            "and RATE its scan",
            "speed. Cutups uses",
            "LANE and ADV instead.",
            "Quad reserves these",
            "stack controls."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Stack movement",
          "lines": [
            "Each voice follows its",
            "own path through the",
            "available lanes.",
            "Pressure offsets",
            "that voice when",
            "Pressure is Offset.",
            "",
            "Loop holds the",
            "current lane",
            "positions, including",
            "blends. Press again",
            "to resume. Note",
            "release keeps a held",
            "position for",
            "retriggering.",
            "",
            "Stack Path offers the",
            "route. For DRAW, click",
            "the main encoder to",
            "edit its points. Back",
            "returns. Cutups",
            "advances lanes by",
            "cuts; Loop pauses",
            "that advancement."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Engine guide",
          "lines": [
            "Choose an engine on",
            "the Engine page. Its",
            "parameter pages",
            "follow the current",
            "editing focus.",
            "",
            "MOTION: moving stacks.",
            "LANES: layer blends.",
            "GRAINS: short grains.",
            "CUTUPS: cut and",
            "repeat. SAMPLE: direct",
            "playback. SLICES:",
            "playable slices.",
            "GLITCH: buffer",
            "stutters. WEAVE: long",
            "grains. WAVESETS:",
            "zero-crossing",
            "segments. PRISM:",
            "spectral playback.",
            "MORPH: spectral blends",
            "and Imprint. TEXTURE:",
            "grouped grains.",
            "FORMANT:",
            "pitch-synchronous",
            "grains.",
            "",
            "Sample/Slices RATE",
            "position is reserved.",
            "",
            "Sample/Slices: lane",
            "is chosen at note-on.",
            "Lane bars follow the",
            "reader, not scan.",
            "Each playhead marks",
            "its own lane.",
            "",
            "Use the online manual",
            "for each engine",
            "parameter."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Stochastic",
          "lines": [
            "STOCH deforms",
            "recorded samples.",
            "AMUT adds polarity",
            "inversion and folding.",
            "TMUT stretches the",
            "internal shape",
            "deeply.",
            "",
            "EVOL sets walk",
            "speed; maximum CYC",
            "advances each",
            "fragment cycle.",
            "Zero holds the",
            "walks. MEM retains",
            "movement; PULL",
            "restores shape.",
            "",
            "Click main encoder",
            "on the Stochastic",
            "page: hold/resume",
            "source. Notes,",
            "deformation and",
            "stack scan",
            "continue. New",
            "notes reuse it.",
            "",
            "Shift+pad holds a",
            "note; Pads",
            "HOLD=MAN keeps it",
            "on until toggled",
            "off. Loop holds",
            "stack scan."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Listener capture",
          "lines": [
            "Stochastic LAW LSTN",
            "makes knob 6 CAPT.",
            "Raise it to settle",
            "mutation/evolution.",
            "PULL keeps its own",
            "saved value.",
            "",
            "AMUT/TMUT set depth;",
            "EVOL sets the clock.",
            "Capture builds fast",
            "and releases slowly.",
            "It keeps some motion.",
            "",
            "Listens to this part",
            "before level/effects.",
            "Pitch, source hold,",
            "and stack scan stay",
            "independent."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pulsar",
          "lines": [
            "PULSAR repeats short",
            "sampled fragments.",
            "Pads pitch the pulse",
            "clock. RATE is Hz",
            "at Root. FORM sets",
            "pulse duration:",
            "1 Hz means 1000 ms.",
            "500 Hz means 2 ms.",
            "",
            "SIZE: 0.5-1000 ms",
            "of source audio",
            "inside each pulse.",
            "WIN/SKEW shape it.",
            "OMIT skips pulses;",
            "BRST adds rests.",
            "JITT varies timing.",
            "",
            "Click main encoder",
            "to hold/resume",
            "source.",
            "Stack scan continues.",
            "Shift+pad with HOLD",
            "MAN latches notes.",
            "",
            "Footer: pulse ms.",
            "~ Root estimate.",
            "LIMIT: overlap is",
            "bounded. Raise FORM",
            "or lower RATE/JITT.",
            "Existing pulses finish",
            "through live edits.",
            "",
            "For a full 1000 ms:",
            "FORM 1, SIZE 1000,",
            "RATE 0.5-2 at Root,",
            "JITT 0. Higher notes",
            "can shorten pulses."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pulsar Mod",
          "lines": [
            "Second Pulsar page.",
            "ERAT/EDEP move the",
            "emission clock.",
            "FRAT/FDEP move FORM.",
            "Rate controls are Hz;",
            "depths are semitones.",
            "",
            "SPRY scatters source",
            "inside Field, around",
            "the current or held",
            "source point.",
            "FVAR varies FORM",
            "per pulse. REV%",
            "reverses sample",
            "reading direction.",
            "",
            "KEYT tracks FORM",
            "with keyboard pitch.",
            "100% gives full",
            "tracking, 0% fixed.",
            "",
            "Amounts default zero.",
            "Edits work on held",
            "notes. Each new pulse",
            "takes new settings;",
            "older pulses finish."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Instrument modes",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Choose a mode",
          "lines": [
            "Hold Capture and",
            "press Menu. Release",
            "Capture, choose Mode,",
            "then",
            "click the desired mode",
            "to apply. Stop",
            "recording first.",
            "",
            "Outside clip and chain",
            "editors, Copy toggles",
            "Single and the last",
            "selected",
            "multi-instrument mode."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Single and Split",
          "lines": [
            "Single: all four lanes",
            "form one stack, with",
            "up to eight voices.",
            "",
            "Split: left and right",
            "pad halves play A and",
            "B. A uses lanes 1-2; B",
            "uses 3-4. Each side",
            "has four voices and",
            "its own engine",
            "settings.",
            "",
            "Tap Capture to",
            "change editing focus.",
            "Waveform knob 8 is",
            "BLND in dual modes;",
            "its midpoint includes",
            "both parts."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Shared Dual / Quad",
          "lines": [
            "Shared Dual: A and B",
            "use the same four",
            "source lanes with",
            "independent engines",
            "and settings. Each",
            "side has four voices.",
            "",
            "Quad: four pad",
            "quadrants play A-D,",
            "with two voices each",
            "and one lane per",
            "part. Track 1-4",
            "selects the part and",
            "lane.",
            "",
            "Tap Capture to cycle",
            "focus. Playing another",
            "part does not change",
            "editing focus."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Levels and effects",
          "lines": [
            "In multi modes, each",
            "part has its own",
            "level, mute and",
            "private processing.",
            "Delay and Reverb use",
            "shared sends and",
            "returns. Tape and",
            "mastering are shared.",
            "",
            "Capture + Menu opens",
            "the page hub. Choose",
            "MIX/FX, then FX SENDS",
            "for A/B sends,",
            "Priority, Curve and",
            "Blend. Delay/Reverb",
            "MIX sets each return;",
            "raise both send and",
            "MIX to hear it.",
            "",
            "Priority Duck lets A",
            "duck B or B duck A.",
            "PRIO sets direction",
            "and depth; THR sets",
            "the trigger level.",
            "Main click opens its",
            "timing/route page.",
            "Quad bypasses it.",
            "",
            "Mute toggles the",
            "focused part. In dual",
            "modes, check Blend and",
            "the part level if a",
            "side becomes silent.",
            "",
            "Tape MIX aligns dry",
            "and wet timing. FMT",
            "and AGE keep channel",
            "timing linked.",
            "MECH, CRNK and INRT",
            "add transport motion."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Performance loops",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Record and play",
          "lines": [
            "Record captures",
            "notes, pressure, stack",
            "holds and knob",
            "movements as data.",
            "Shift + Record",
            "captures audio",
            "instead.",
            "",
            "Choose Replace or",
            "Overdub on",
            "Performance Loop.",
            "Press Record to",
            "start and again to",
            "finish. Notes already",
            "held are included.",
            "Play stops or starts",
            "the loop.",
            "",
            "All parts share one",
            "recorder. Rate",
            "changes performance",
            "speed; the source",
            "samples remain",
            "separate."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Undo an overdub",
          "lines": [
            "Overdub adds a take",
            "to the existing loop",
            "without changing its",
            "length.",
            "",
            "Finish recording with",
            "Record. Hold Delete",
            "and press Record to",
            "remove the newest",
            "overdub. Repeat for",
            "earlier passes. The",
            "base take is",
            "protected.",
            "",
            "The curved-arrow",
            "Undo key handles the",
            "latest protected",
            "sample, clip or chain",
            "edit instead."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Clips and chains",
          "lines": [
            "Step 1-16 selects a",
            "clip in the current",
            "bank. From waveform",
            "or parameter views,",
            "Left/Right selects",
            "banks A-D. Each clip",
            "owns its performance,",
            "settings and four",
            "sample assignments.",
            "",
            "Shift + Play cycles",
            "Clip Overview, Chain",
            "and waveform. In",
            "Chain, Step keys",
            "select chain entries;",
            "Left/Right selects",
            "entry pages.",
            "",
            "Chain entries choose",
            "clips, repeats and",
            "fade behavior. Chain",
            "bank stores multiple",
            "chains. End can Loop,",
            "Stay or Stop",
            "transport."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pattern fades",
          "lines": [
            "Pattern Fade blends",
            "two playing clips,",
            "including their",
            "samples and settings.",
            "TIME reaches 30",
            "seconds; CUT changes",
            "immediately.",
            "",
            "FIX sets one",
            "duration. RAND",
            "chooses between LOW",
            "and HIGH. CURVE",
            "shapes the blend.",
            "",
            "Touch knob 3 to",
            "engage Hold; turn",
            "XFADE to move",
            "manually. Releasing",
            "touch keeps Hold on.",
            "Main click resumes.",
            "DONE commits the",
            "destination."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Shortcuts / safety",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Capture gestures",
          "lines": [
            "Hold Capture for",
            "bottom-row",
            "performance pads.",
            "Pads 1-4 grab lanes;",
            "pads 5-8 apply DARK,",
            "CRSH, ECHO and SPCE.",
            "Pressure changes",
            "strength. Release",
            "restores the current",
            "settings.",
            "",
            "Available lanes follow",
            "the part; Quad has no",
            "lane rides. Shift +",
            "Capture saves",
            "Schwung Skipback",
            "audio."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Copy and clear",
          "lines": [
            "Shift + Step copies",
            "the current clip to",
            "that destination.",
            "Delete + Step resets",
            "the destination clip",
            "and its sources.",
            "",
            "In clip and chain",
            "views, Copy copies a",
            "recorded clip; Shift +",
            "Copy pastes. In Chain,",
            "paste creates an",
            "independent clip for",
            "the selected entry.",
            "",
            "Outside the reports,",
            "Shift + Delete clears",
            "the selected audio",
            "lane. Stop recording",
            "before Undo.",
            "",
            "Stop playback before",
            "pasting over the",
            "current clip."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Undo and panic",
          "lines": [
            "The curved-arrow",
            "Undo key restores",
            "the latest protected",
            "sample, clip or chain",
            "edit. Stop recording",
            "first.",
            "",
            "Hold Delete and press",
            "Play for Panic. It",
            "stops the",
            "performance and",
            "releases notes,",
            "latches, Rolls and",
            "preview. Effect tails",
            "decay. Audio-lane",
            "recording continues."
